<file path="web/README.md">
# einvoicecheck.ae - marketing site

Next.js 15 (App Router, TypeScript) marketing site for the UAE e-invoice **preflight
validation** API. Deploys to Railway (project `einvoicecheck.ae`, env `production`).

## Positioning guardrail (non-negotiable)

Preflight validation only. The copy must never claim FTA accreditation, transmission of
legal e-invoices, replacement of an accredited service provider, or statutory archival.
The guardrail sentence lives in `src/lib/site.ts` (`GUARDRAIL`) and is rendered by
`<GuardrailNotice />` on every commercial page plus the footer of every page. Keep it there.

## Run

```bash
npm install
npm run dev     # http://localhost:3000
npm run build   # production build (type-checked)
npm start
```

## Routes

| Route | Purpose | Primary keyword |
|-------|---------|-----------------|
| `/` | Homepage | `e invoicing UAE` |
| `/pricing` | Free trial / $29 / $99. Billing NOT live. | `UAE e invoicing software` |
| `/docs` | API docs skeleton, mirrors `handoffs/E1/openapi.yaml` | `UAE e invoicing API` |
| `/blog` | Content hub, 8-week plan in `src/lib/posts.ts` | supporting |
| `/waitlist` | Signup capture -> `POST /api/waitlist` | - |
| `/alternatives/[slug]` | **Reserved for M2.** cleartax, comarch, sovos | `FTA approved accounting software in UAE` |
| `/vs/[slug]` | **Reserved for M2.** cleartax, comarch, sovos | comparison intent |
| `/tools/[slug]` | **Reserved for GR1's free tool.** Drop the tool into the `TODO(GR1)` slot. | `PINT AE validation` (+ `e invoicing UAE`) |
| `/sitemap.xml`, `/robots.txt` | Generated by `src/app/sitemap.ts` / `robots.ts` | - |

## Billing

**Dodo Payments**, wired up in step E2. Not live. No payment SDK is embedded anywhere in
this repo and no card details are collected. `/pricing` says so explicitly.

## Waitlist store

`src/app/api/waitlist/route.ts` appends JSON lines to `WAITLIST_STORE_PATH`
(default `./data/waitlist.jsonl`). This is a **stub** - the container filesystem on Railway
is ephemeral. `TODO(E2)`: swap for the real datastore + auth + Dodo checkout handoff.

## Env

See `.env.example` - names only, no secrets, no credentials committed.
</file>

